#let course_description = [
  This honors seminar is the first part of a two course Honors sequence. The students will work on a full year individual original research project. Students will follow complete practices of research reproducibility and open science. The first semester will be a review of research practices and tools, and will result in the identification of a research question. The second semester will be based on carrying out an original data science project. The result will be a hybrid product with a 20-25 page (5000 - 6000 words) research paper, with data visualizations and analysis tables, along with a documented data source, annotated code, well  documented GitHub repository, and open science posting of the project.
  
  Students will work together during the class to review each other's code, documentation and reproducibility practices. Seminar time will be a combination of discussing readings, investigating approaches to research, and discussing data visualization and presentation of results. The seminar will be collaborative in discussing and reviewing best practices in Data Science.
  
  The expectation for the Fall Semester H195A course is that students will be able to confirm their advisor and dataset during the Fall semester.  Not all students will move on from H195A to H195B. Failure to make progress on the data that will be analyzed and the advisor that will work with you will result in not being able to enroll in H195B and graduate with Honors.  
]

