== Safe Space Classroom

All students are expected to respect one another in addition to respecting the instructor. This respect includes, but is not limited to, active listening to peers' discussions or questions and openness to all discussion points/questions. Being accepting of other discussion points does not mean that you must agree with those points, but this should lead to respectful discussions and not attacking one another. 

Some examples of unacceptable disrespective behaviors:

1. "That is a stupid question."

2. "Are you kidding? We just went over that."

3. Nonverbal cues of not paying attention or eye rolling

== Attendance & Participation

All students are expected to come to every class. Additionally, *GET USED TO TALKING*. This course will be part lecture and part seminar. This means that I will talk through some slides on each week's topic with points of discussions, but we will also work in small groups, and talking through our project idea. If you cannot make the class, it is the student's responsibility to email me to let me know they won't make it to class. 

== Course Conflicts & Video Recordings

For those students that have course conflicts, I expect you to attend this course. I will record lectures, but I will *not* post them on bCourses unless there are unexpected circumstances or the student and I agree to an arrangement. If a midterm and/or final exam overlaps with this course, it is the student's responsibility to work out an arrangement with the instructor.

